  "details": "previously you could download a addon for Unity that would make script compiles happen in realtime (it wasnt made for vrchat development specifically but yk still worked with vrchat)\n\nhaving realtime script compiles would allow you to compile the scripts in editor during play mode making development faster instead of having to wait for compiling as before the Persistence update addons that would allow compiling to happen like this was imo super helpful as it shaved off at times minutes of waiting so the options for this would probably just be\n\nA. make persistence not be so bad within Editor so previous addons can work normally (Better)\n\nB. directly support direct/ realtime compiling (Optimal)\n\nC. make persistence shenanigans not affect literally everything in Editor (persistence can be unused in any user made code and it'll still prevent realtime compiles from working properly, imo it super annoying that it is the way it is) (Bandaid fix)\n\nrealtime compiling would be (imo) a really nice QOL",
